WEBVTT

00:00:02.000 --> 00:00:03.720
Every trial comes with an end date.

00:00:03.970 --> 00:00:06.090
I study the ones that keep going anyway.

00:00:06.590 --> 00:00:10.537
Dr Lindiwe Achterberg lectures in our School of Emergent Priorities.

00:00:10.937 --> 00:00:13.647
I used to evaluate pilots for a state agency.

00:00:13.847 --> 00:00:15.927
Hardly any of them ever concluded.

00:00:16.427 --> 00:00:18.006
A demountable classroom,

00:00:18.106 --> 00:00:19.906
still temporary decades on.

00:00:20.206 --> 00:00:22.676
Relocated bus stops and pop-up lanes.

00:00:22.776 --> 00:00:25.146
Only nine per cent closed on schedule.

00:00:25.646 --> 00:00:29.306
Her research funding is the third-highest at Slop University.

00:00:29.906 --> 00:00:31.717
More than eight hundred thousand dollars,

00:00:31.918 --> 00:00:34.958
from two Anticipatory Capability Fund grants.

00:00:35.208 --> 00:00:37.338
And a hundred and ninety-eight research outputs,

00:00:37.438 --> 00:00:38.938
the third most in her School.

00:00:39.538 --> 00:00:41.638
A trial should end with a decision.

00:00:41.888 --> 00:00:43.648
Even if the decision is to keep it.

00:00:45.248 --> 00:00:47.208
Every one of her outputs is on our website.

00:00:47.358 --> 00:00:48.378
We're on Bluesky,

00:00:48.528 --> 00:00:49.898
and you can reach us by email.
